Usage: polyglot validator [-hqv] [--header-file=<headerFile>] json_proxy
Validate a json proxy
      json_proxy   json file of the proxy
  -h, --help       display sub-command usage and exit
      --header-file=<headerFile>
                   append the content of the given file to all sources
                     generated by Polyglot.
  -q               be quiet
  -v               verbose output


Running `polyglot ada2proxy --help`
================================================================================

Usage: polyglot ada2proxy [OPTIONS]
Create a proxy for the given Ada project.
If no unit is explicitly passed through --spec-files, generate bindings for all
sources of the project tree, including those of the subprojects, but not those
of the Ada runtime.
If --process-runtime is set, also generate bindings for all the sources of the
runtime.
If --no-subprojects is set, only generate bindings for the root project.
Note that --process-runtime and --no-subprojects are illegal as soon as
--spec-files is used.
Moreover, please note that polyglot will always make sure that the generated
library is usable, which means it may have to include entities that were not
part of the original files.
  -P=project_file           input GPR project file
  -o, --output=<outputPath> output path for the proxy project
      --spec-files=<specFiles>[,<specFiles>...]
                            filenames of the units of the input project to
                              bind, separated by commas
  -X=<scenarioVariables>    Scenario variables to pass to the project file
      --RTS=<rts>           Name of the runtime (RTS) to use when loading the
                              project
      --target=<target>     Specify a target for cross platforms
      --no-subprojects      Only process units of the root project
      --process-runtime     Also process the sources of the Ada runtime
      --with-runtime=<withRuntime>
                            location of the polyglot runtime to use. Defaults
                              to <outputPath>/runtimes
  -h, --help                display sub-command usage and exit
      --header-file=<headerFile>
                            append the content of the given file to all sources
                              generated by Polyglot.
  -q                        be quiet
  -v                        verbose output


Running `polyglot proxy2cpp --help`
================================================================================

Usage: polyglot proxy2cpp [-hqv] [--header-file=<headerFile>] -o=<outputPath>
                          proxy_file
Create the C++ interface of a proxy representation
      proxy_file   input proxy json file
  -h, --help       display sub-command usage and exit
      --header-file=<headerFile>
                   append the content of the given file to all sources
                     generated by Polyglot.
  -o, --output=<outputPath>
                   path to the directory in which the C++ interface should be
                     generated. Directories along the path are created if they
                     do not exist yet.
  -q               be quiet
  -v               verbose output


